---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import SectionDots from '../components/SectionDots.astro';

const principles = [
  {
    title: '1. Self-contained',
    description:
      "A communication engine is always self-contained, meaning it can operate by itself and doesn't require the presence of other containers to service.",
  },
  {
    title: '2. Lightweight',
    description:
      'A communication engine is not a big silo but a microservice. It must implement a specific function that can serve a wider workload.',
  },
  {
    title: '3. Remotely managed',
    description:
      'Communication engines must always expose remote management capabilities; configuration files, configuration APIs or web interface for manual intervention.',
  },
  {
    title: '4. Auditable',
    description:
      'A communication engine provides the tools to audit its health and its behavior. An example of common audit tools are CDRs, Alarms logs or Audit logs.',
  },
  {
    title: '5. Follow industry standards',
    description: 'Must follow OpenAPI industry standard and must comply with the 3GPP common API framework.',
  },
  {
    title: '6. High level of customization',
    description:
      'Communication engines implementing a telecom protocol must provide the ability to customize its protocol stack to adapt to various use cases.',
  },
];

const components = [
  { title: 'Light HTTP server', description: 'Used by communication engines to expose an API or a Graphical UI.' },
  { title: 'Async HTTP client', description: 'Used by communication engines that needs to issue HTTP requests.' },
  { title: 'React UI library', description: 'A set of react components reused across engines single page web GUI.' },
  { title: 'CAPIF library', description: 'A library of CAPIF API requires for API Invokers and API Providers.' },
  { title: 'SIP library', description: 'Provides the SIP & MRFC protocol stack.' },
  { title: 'DIAMETER library', description: 'Provides the DIAMETER protocol stack.' },
  { title: 'GTP library', description: 'Provides GTP-C v1 GTP-C v2 protocol stack.' },
  { title: 'RADIUS library', description: 'Provides a client/server RADIUS protocol stack.' },
  { title: 'SMPP library', description: 'Provides ESME SMPP v3.4/v5.0 protocol stack.' },
  { title: 'SS7 library', description: 'Contains all the SS7 protocol stack; SCTP, M3UA, SCCP, TCAP, MAP, CAP and INAP.' },
  { title: 'Common library', description: 'Contains common framework libraries such as logging, caching, JSON and SNMP.' },
  { title: 'Data access library', description: 'Provides data access component for engines that requires storage of noSQL docs.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Technology"
  description="Slicce develops microservices that focus on performing specific tasks on top of the telecom core network."
>
  <PageBanner title="Technology" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container tech-intro">
      <p>
        Slicce develops microservices that focus on performing specific tasks on top of the telecom core network.
        These microservices are called cloud communication engines. The communication engines can either stand by
        themselves or be deployed with others in a workload. A workload is a set of containers or pods put together
        to construct a solution, platform or service. The cloud communication engines are divided into four
        categories: API Exposure Functions (AEF), Application Functions (AF), Inter-Working Functions (IWF) and Load
        Balancers (LB). Slicce's architecture relies on OpenAPIs to communicate between microservices. Therefore, it
        also delivers a 3GPP Common API Framework Core Function (CAPIF-CF) to harmonize the communication between the
        microservices in a standard way and allow API exposure for 3G, 4G and 5G northbound APIs. All the cloud
        communication engines, regardless of their category, rely on one same foundation: the slicce cloud
        communication engine foundation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <SectionDots count={4} active={1} />
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">The slicce cloud communication engine foundation</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        All slicce communication engines follow the same design principles and use one same foundation. This eases
        not only the maintenance of the microservices but also enables a faster creation of new microservices. Here
        are some of the foundation principles:
      </p>
      <div class="rows">
        {
          principles.map((p) => (
            <div class="row">
              <div class="row__label">
                <h3>{p.title}</h3>
                <span class="divider" />
              </div>
              <p>{p.description}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

    </div>
    <div class="diagram-band">
      <div class="container">
        <img
          src="/images/products/slicce-engine.drawio.svg"
          alt="Cloud communication engine foundation architecture diagram"
          width="822"
          height="351"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionDots count={3} active={2} />

      <p class="section-intro">
        The foundation components are reusable across cloud communication engines to reduce the time of development
        of a new microservices:
      </p>
      <div class="grid">
        {
          components.map((c) => (
            <div class="entry">
              <h3>{c.title}</h3>
              <span class="divider" />
              <p>{c.description}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--gray">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="quote">
        In the heart of the foundation the 3GPP Common API framework facilitates<br />
        communication exchanges using APIs across the workload's microservices.
      </p>
      <div class="diagram">
        <img
          src="/images/products/slicce-capif.drawio.svg"
          alt="3GPP Common API Framework at the heart of the foundation diagram"
          width="882"
          height="462"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container valuable">
      <img src="/images/icons/question-heptagon-outline.png" alt="" width="190" height="152" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
        <h2>What makes the cloud communication engine foundation valuable?</h2>
        <p>
          It brings us the ability to rapidly develop new communication engines that adds more value. This is done by
          applying the common microservices architecture and by re-using the existing libraries to reach stability and
          production level very rapidly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-12);
  }

  .section--gray {
    background: var(--color-section-gray);
  }

  .tech-intro p {
    text-align: justify;
  }

  .section-title {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .section-intro {
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-12);
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 18.667px;
  }

  .rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-12);
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
    column-gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .row__label h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .row p {
    max-width: 700px;
    font-size: 14.667px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .divider {
    display: block;
    width: 56px;
    height: 4px;
    background: var(--color-green);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    column-gap: var(--space-8);
    row-gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .entry h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .entry p {
    font-size: 14.667px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .quote {
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 18.667px;
  }

  .diagram-band {
    background: var(--color-section-gray);
    padding-block: var(--space-12);
  }

  .diagram-band .container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .diagram {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .diagram img,
  .diagram-band img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 800px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .valuable {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .valuable img {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .valuable h2 {
    font-size: 26px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: var(--space-3);
    }

    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .valuable {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
